# Generated. All of it is reproducible from fetch.py / local.py + prepare.py
# + migrate.py, and it is big: a single 52-run pass left 2.9G in runs2/ and
# 1.7G in cache/.
#
# The globs are suffixed deliberately. An earlier version listed `work/` and
# `cache/` exactly, so `work-vv2/` and `runs2/` - the directories an actual
# run creates once tasks come from more than one source - matched nothing and
# 3G of checked-out repositories sat staged behind `??  bench/`.
#
# `migrated/` was the same miss one commit later: it holds rewritten articles
# from whatever corpus was benchmarked, so what leaks is somebody else's
# private knowledge base rather than just disk.
cache*/
work*/
runs*/
migrated*/
rubrics*/
tasks*.json
results*.json
scores*.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
